course: dictionary
lesson: 5645
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word lion is a good example. «In The Lion King, Simba is a young lion who will become king.» Here lion is a real animal, because a young lion can grow up to be a king of the animals.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The Great Sphinx is a huge statue with a lion's body and a pharaoh's head» tells you the lion is a body shape, not a brave person. The clue is statue, so the meaning is the animal.
explain: When someone is called brave as a lion, lion is a symbol of courage and strength. Ask yourself: does the sentence still make sense if I put a real animal in its place? If it doesn't, the word is probably being used with its second meaning.
fact: A lion is a big wild cat with golden fur that lives mostly in Africa.
fact: The male lion has a large mane, which is a thick ring of hair around its head.
fact: Lions live in groups called prides, and the lionesses do most of the hunting.
fact: A lion is also a symbol of courage and strength.
fact: «Simba» means lion in Swahili, a language of East Africa.
exercise: In «Serengeti lions rest on rocky outcrops called kopjes», what is a lion? | A rocky hill | A brave and strong person | *A big wild cat with golden fur | A small mouse
exercise: «He fought like a lion to save his team.» What does lion mean here? | A group of animals | A golden cat in the zoo | A rocky hill | *Courage and strength
exercise: What is a group of lions called? | A swarm | A herd | *A pride | A flock
test: What is a mane? | A kind of call | A type of grass | *A thick ring of hair around the head | A large cave
test: A lion is a symbol of courage and strength. What is a symbol? | *Something that stands for an idea | A loud noise | A kind of statue only | A sum for maths
exam: «The Great Sphinx is a huge statue with a lion's body and a pharaoh's head.» Does lion mean a real animal here? | A pride of lions | The biggest share of something | A brave person | *The animal's body shape, carved in stone
